   218	## 11. The design phase
   219	
   220	The work is an architecture POC: the design page, one PRD per module and the decisions. No product code and no data
   221	files until Alex starts the build. `docs/check.py` checks (and rebuilds the PRD bundle the page reads from disk); the
   222	only other scripts generate page assets (`build_bundle.py`, `copy_old_design.py`, `embed_fonts.py`) or simulate
   223	classification (`simulate_classification.py`, not changed at this stage).
   224	
   225	- The design page is `docs/system-design.html` with its data in `docs/system-design/new-*.js`; each module's PRD is in
   226	  `docs/prd/` (index `README.md`). The page data is the one source: a PRD block marked `generated` comes from it and
   227	  is never edited by hand.
   228	- After any change, refresh by reasoning: re-read every module in the order and with the four questions of
   229	  `docs/prd/README.md` (D22), so that page, PRD and decisions say the same thing, and list each inconsistency fixed.
   230	  `python3 docs/check.py` runs last and checks only mechanically; its pass is never the refresh.
